-- Ekwo OS — Sierra Leone: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/sl at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build sl`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Goods and Services Tax Act, 2009 (Act No. 6 of 2009), Supplement to the Sierra Leone Gazette Vol. CXL, No. 37 of 20 August 2009: ss. 8 to 10 (taxable, exempt and zero-rated supply), 14 (imposition and the 15 per cent rate), 15 (registration threshold), 24 (reverse charge on imported services), 27 (net amount of GST), 28 and 29 (input tax credits), 31 (GST invoices), 37 to 40 (returns, payment, imports); First, Second, Third and Fourth Schedules (Parliament of Sierra Leone, as published in the Sierra Leone Gazette)
--     https://www.sierra-leone.org/Laws/2009-06.pdf
--   The Finance Act, 2023 — s. 5 (digital services, amending s. 8(h) of the GST Act), s. 6 (the Second Schedule of the GST Act, exempt supplies, repealed and replaced by 25 items) and s. 7 (a 2 per cent tourism levy collected under the GST Act's filing and payment rules, paid by the 15th of the following month); the copy consulted is the Bill supplement to the Gazette of 28 March 2023 and states that the Act operates from 1 April 2023 (Government of Sierra Leone, as published in the Sierra Leone Gazette)
--     https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/sl/2023/sl-government-gazette-supplement-dated-2023-03-28-no-15.pdf
--   Goods & Services Tax — the single 15 per cent rate, the four categories of supply, zero-rated and exempt examples, GST invoice contents, returns and payment not later than the end of the month following the tax period, the tax period, returns in leones (National Revenue Authority of Sierra Leone)
--     https://mail.nra.gov.sl/node/128
--   Domestic Taxes & Rates — the Authority's table of rates and due dates (withholding tax, PAYE, payroll tax, rent tax and the other taxes this pack documents and does not compute) (National Revenue Authority of Sierra Leone)
--     https://mail.nra.gov.sl/node/131
--   Electronic Cash Register — s. 34 of the GST Act as replaced by s. 34 of the Finance Act 2020: every registered GST business keeps an electronic cash register specified by the Commissioner-General, made of a Certified Invoicing System and a Sales Data Controller that signs each receipt and sends it to the Authority's server (National Revenue Authority of Sierra Leone)
--     https://mail.nra.gov.sl/node/916
--   ITAS — the Authority's Domestic Tax Information System, the taxpayer portal for registration, returns and payments (National Revenue Authority of Sierra Leone)
--     https://itas.nra.gov.sl
--   Sierra Leone — use of IFRS Standards: IFRS Standards required of listed companies, banks and insurers; IFRS for SMEs adopted by CSAAG resolution BPR2/2009 and permitted for other entities; standards set by CSAAG under authority delegated by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sierra Leone (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/sierra-leone/
